WEBVTT

﻿1
00:01:04.147 --> 00:01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

2
00:01:08.943 --> 00:01:09.861
Well,

3
00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.238
we have a house

4
00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:14.908
and even a boat.

5
00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:18.161
This is insane.

6
00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:21.164
You happy?

7
00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:22.290
Yeah.

8
00:01:24.626 --> 00:01:25.877
I am, Gwan-sik.

9
00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.223
Uh, stop!

10
00:01:48.983 --> 00:01:52.695
<i>It was our brightest season,</i>
<i>and it would never return.</i>

11
00:01:55.198 --> 00:01:59.369
LIFE GOES ON AND ON

12
00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.979
HALLIM DISASTER RELIEF
DEPUTY CHIEF OH AE-SUN

13
00:02:33.611 --> 00:02:35.321
BABY FORMULA

14
00:02:47.375 --> 00:02:49.210
You've got to live up to your title.

15
00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:50.670
Okay?

16
00:02:56.759 --> 00:02:58.928
I'm the deputy chief, after all.

17
00:02:59.429 --> 00:03:02.015
Let's just add two more.

18
00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:21.242
Oh, for goodness' sake.

19
00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:26.873
I told you I'd give you candy
after your food was done, didn't I?

20
00:03:26.956 --> 00:03:29.167
Why don't you ever listen to Mommy?

21
00:03:29.751 --> 00:03:32.128
- Goodness gracious.
- Mommy, give me a hug.

22
00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:34.172
Give me a hug.

23
00:03:34.255 --> 00:03:38.676
Mommy, I want a hug.
Mommy, Mommy, give me a hug.

24
00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.470
Mommy! Mommy!

25
00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:43.556
Ms. Oh! Ms. Oh!
Geum-myeong is in trouble! She's hurt!

26
00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.141
- Mommy!
- What?

27
00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:46.476
Mommy!

28
00:03:49.145 --> 00:03:51.314
Is she bleeding? Tell me! Tell me!

29
00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:53.441
I don't know. It's this way.

30
00:03:55.193 --> 00:03:58.738
Auntie! Auntie!
Can you watch my kids for me?

31
00:03:58.821 --> 00:04:00.323
Huh?

32
00:04:33.523 --> 00:04:35.984
Are you the sea god's daughter? Are you?

33
00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:38.194
Look, even the dolphins are running away.

34
00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:40.154
How can you ride in a typhoon?

35
00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.366
It's the motorbike that hit me,
not the other way around.

36
00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:47.078
Jeju winds can flip over cars.

37
00:04:47.161 --> 00:04:49.872
Your little bike here
would flip over again and again.

38
00:04:50.373 --> 00:04:51.207
Gosh.

39
00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:00.216
Auntie!

40
00:05:02.593 --> 00:05:03.761
Auntie!

41
00:05:09.058 --> 00:05:10.226
Auntie!

42
00:05:11.394 --> 00:05:12.603
Where are the boys?

43
00:05:14.772 --> 00:05:16.607
Are they sleeping in our house?

44
00:05:16.691 --> 00:05:18.526
Huh? The boys?

45
00:05:28.411 --> 00:05:29.704
Eun-myeong!

46
00:05:31.414 --> 00:05:34.876
So why did you leave the boys behind?
It wasn't even a major accident.

47
00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:37.962
- Eun-myeong. Honey! Oh no.
- Eun-myeong!

48
00:05:38.046 --> 00:05:39.380
- Dong-myeong!
- Dong-myeong!

49
00:05:39.464 --> 00:05:41.299
- Dong-myeong!
- Honey!

50
00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:44.010
Dong-myeong!

51
00:05:44.093 --> 00:05:46.095
Eun-myeong! Eun-myeong!

52
00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.015
Eun-myeong! Eun-myeong!

53
00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:58.149
How many times did Grandma warn you

54
00:05:58.232 --> 00:06:01.194
that once the boys start running,
they'll go anywhere, huh?

55
00:06:01.277 --> 00:06:02.653
Hey, their shoes.

56
00:06:03.654 --> 00:06:05.281
Their shoes are not here.

57
00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.075
What?

58
00:06:07.909 --> 00:06:09.702
I'll go look in the cabbage field and…

59
00:06:09.786 --> 00:06:12.580
- Ae-sun, pay me for seaweed.
- …and, Mom, look around…

60
00:06:13.164 --> 00:06:15.917
I didn't harvest all the seaweed
I was going to

61
00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:18.920
because I found your biggest boy here.

62
00:06:19.003 --> 00:06:20.421
Goodness gracious.

63
00:06:20.922 --> 00:06:21.881
Oh!

64
00:06:22.382 --> 00:06:25.009
I told you not to move and stay here,
didn't I?

65
00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:29.889
He was standing alone on the seawall,
afraid and desperately looking for you.

66
00:06:29.972 --> 00:06:31.057
Why did you leave?

67
00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.643
Why did you go to
such a dangerous area alone?

68
00:06:34.143 --> 00:06:36.270
The truck auntie would've come for you.

69
00:06:36.354 --> 00:06:38.064
Why couldn't you just wait?

70
00:06:38.147 --> 00:06:39.232
Why?

71
00:06:39.315 --> 00:06:42.735
If you stand there,
the waves will swallow you up.

72
00:06:42.819 --> 00:06:45.363
Cows get swept up by Jeju typhoons.

73
00:06:45.446 --> 00:06:47.073
You have to be careful.

74
00:06:48.157 --> 00:06:49.367
Where's Dong-myeong?

75
00:06:52.662 --> 00:06:54.288
Where's Dong-myeong?

76
00:06:54.372 --> 00:06:55.206
At home.

77
00:06:55.957 --> 00:06:58.167
Wasn't Dong-myeong with you
this whole time?

78
00:07:00.378 --> 00:07:01.879
He's home!

79
00:07:04.882 --> 00:07:07.635
What are you telling me? Stop scaring me.

80
00:07:08.136 --> 00:07:10.304
Mommy, give me a hug.

81
00:07:10.388 --> 00:07:14.058
- Give me a hug. Mommy, I want a hug.
- Is she bleeding? Tell me. Tell me!

82
00:07:14.142 --> 00:07:16.769
Mommy. Mommy.

83
00:07:49.302 --> 00:07:50.428
Geum-myeong,

84
00:07:51.888 --> 00:07:53.347
go call the chief's office.

85
00:08:05.026 --> 00:08:07.069
Who can stop
the whims of summer?

86
00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:11.032
Yesterday, it was bright and sunny,
like a bride on her wedding day.

87
00:08:11.699 --> 00:08:14.744
And today, it gets aggressive
like when your wife loses her temper.

88
00:08:15.244 --> 00:08:17.455
At least you can always get
a new wife…

89
00:08:17.538 --> 00:08:19.499
…but when summer screws you over…

90
00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:22.168
Goddamn it.

91
00:08:22.251 --> 00:08:23.586
- Okay.
- Ow!

92
00:08:24.212 --> 00:08:26.214
Oh man.

93
00:08:26.714 --> 00:08:29.425
You can't build a barrier
by running your mouth, right?

94
00:08:30.051 --> 00:08:30.927
Gwan-sik!

95
00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:32.929
Gwan-sik!

96
00:08:39.602 --> 00:08:42.230
- Honey! Dong-myeong!
- Dong-myeong!

97
00:08:42.313 --> 00:08:43.606
Dong-myeong!

98
00:08:45.691 --> 00:08:47.235
Dong-myeong!

99
00:08:47.318 --> 00:08:48.736
Dong-myeong!

100
00:08:50.154 --> 00:08:51.489
- Dong-myeong!
- Dong-myeong!

101
00:08:51.572 --> 00:08:53.199
Yang Dong-myeong!

102
00:08:53.282 --> 00:08:54.659
Dong-myeong!

103
00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:58.246
Dong-myeong!

104
00:08:58.329 --> 00:08:59.539
Dong-myeong!

105
00:09:00.289 --> 00:09:01.832
Dong-myeong!

106
00:09:03.292 --> 00:09:04.168
Dong-myeong!

107
00:09:04.252 --> 00:09:05.920
Dong-myeong!

108
00:09:06.003 --> 00:09:08.381
- Dong-myeong!
- Dong-myeong!

109
00:09:08.464 --> 00:09:10.925
Dong-myeong!

110
00:09:12.718 --> 00:09:14.762
- Dong-myeong!
- Dong-myeong!

111
00:09:15.346 --> 00:09:19.100
Where did he go? Dong-myeong!

112
00:09:20.142 --> 00:09:21.686
Dong-myeong!

113
00:09:23.062 --> 00:09:25.231
Dong-myeong! Honey!

114
00:09:27.358 --> 00:09:29.819
Yang Dong-myeong! Honey!

115
00:09:29.902 --> 00:09:31.112
Where are you?

116
00:09:31.195 --> 00:09:32.196
Dong-myeong!

117
00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:35.866
Dong-myeong! Yang Dong-myeong!

118
00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:38.160
Please have mercy on us.
Please, dear Lord.

119
00:09:38.244 --> 00:09:40.997
Whatever it takes,
save the child for us, dear Lord.

120
00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:42.999
Just save my grandchild.

121
00:09:44.041 --> 00:09:45.668
Send our baby back to us.

122
00:09:47.211 --> 00:09:49.213
Please save the child. Please.

123
00:09:50.256 --> 00:09:52.550
It only takes a second to lose a child.

124
00:09:52.633 --> 00:09:54.135
Please save him. Save my grandbaby.

125
00:09:54.218 --> 00:09:56.804
Do you know what people
all over the world say

126
00:09:57.305 --> 00:09:59.932
at any time they lose their kids?

127
00:10:00.016 --> 00:10:02.268
- Dong-myeong! Honey!
- <i>They all say the same thing.</i>

128
00:10:02.351 --> 00:10:04.562
<i>"It happened in the blink of an eye."</i>

129
00:10:04.645 --> 00:10:07.773
<i>They lost their child</i>
<i>in the blink of an eye.</i>

130
00:10:14.238 --> 00:10:15.698
They found my son? Did they?

131
00:10:17.033 --> 00:10:17.867
Ae-sun.

132
00:10:18.367 --> 00:10:19.577
Did we find my son?

133
00:10:21.996 --> 00:10:22.955
Ae-sun.

134
00:10:28.294 --> 00:10:29.211
Ae-sun.

135
00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:31.672
What?

136
00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:33.758
What?

137
00:11:06.207 --> 00:11:07.291
Hospital.

138
00:11:08.501 --> 00:11:10.670
Dong-myeong needs to see the doctor.

139
00:11:11.921 --> 00:11:12.922
Oh boy.

140
00:11:14.131 --> 00:11:16.258
My baby, he's cold.

141
00:11:19.053 --> 00:11:21.681
Why isn't anyone calling an ambulance?

142
00:11:26.811 --> 00:11:27.728
Dong-myeong.

143
00:11:28.354 --> 00:11:29.188
Honey.

144
00:11:29.939 --> 00:11:30.773
Honey.

145
00:11:31.273 --> 00:11:32.108
Dear.

146
00:11:34.068 --> 00:11:34.902
Dong-myeong.

147
00:11:35.653 --> 00:11:36.570
Baby.

148
00:11:37.571 --> 00:11:38.406
Baby.

149
00:11:39.031 --> 00:11:40.408
What's wrong with you?

150
00:11:42.159 --> 00:11:43.202
Honey.

151
00:11:45.538 --> 00:11:46.580
We need

152
00:11:48.499 --> 00:11:50.835
to call the doctor. The doctor.

153
00:12:03.305 --> 00:12:05.808
Call for an ambulance, okay, Gwan-sik?

154
00:12:06.517 --> 00:12:07.518
Why

155
00:12:08.394 --> 00:12:10.438
won't anyone call for the ambulance?

156
00:12:11.772 --> 00:12:13.941
Just call for the ambulance,
why don't you?

157
00:12:18.988 --> 00:12:21.323
<i>It was the day</i>
<i>their world crashed down.</i>

158
00:12:31.375 --> 00:12:32.752
<i>For the first time…</i>

159
00:12:36.297 --> 00:12:38.674
<i>…their Steelheart broke apart.</i>

160
00:13:39.109 --> 00:13:40.694
<i>My father's tears</i>

161
00:13:41.487 --> 00:13:42.780
<i>filled the seas.</i>

162
00:15:07.406 --> 00:15:09.450
I should've hugged him.

163
00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:16.165
I should've hugged him.

164
00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:20.669
<i>Her son,</i>
<i>who was with her at lunch,</i>

165
00:15:21.670 --> 00:15:23.631
<i>was no more by dinner.</i>

166
00:15:25.925 --> 00:15:28.469
Mommy. Mommy!

167
00:15:28.552 --> 00:15:30.679
Mommy, give me a hug.

168
00:15:30.763 --> 00:15:32.890
Give me a hug.

169
00:15:32.973 --> 00:15:34.725
<i>Mommy, I want a hug.</i>

170
00:15:34.808 --> 00:15:37.561
Mommy, Mommy, give me a hug.

171
00:15:47.905 --> 00:15:49.490
I should've hugged him.

172
00:16:14.848 --> 00:16:16.183
<i>At the funeral,</i>

173
00:16:16.684 --> 00:16:20.145
<i>Grandma never accused Mom of anything.</i>

174
00:16:20.229 --> 00:16:23.273
<i>She just said that a mother</i>
<i>who lost her child</i>

175
00:16:23.357 --> 00:16:25.275
<i>has more tears than the sea.</i>

176
00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:38.914
Move on.

177
00:16:40.165 --> 00:16:41.250
What choice do you have?

178
00:16:42.876 --> 00:16:46.088
You have two children
who still need you to be their mother.

179
00:16:49.842 --> 00:16:51.802
Life will move on if you let it.

180
00:16:52.302 --> 00:16:53.762
Life goes on.

181
00:16:56.015 --> 00:16:57.391
<i>Life goes on.</i>

182
00:16:58.142 --> 00:17:00.561
<i>There will be days when life is hard.</i>

183
00:17:01.854 --> 00:17:04.189
Once in a while, there may be days

184
00:17:04.273 --> 00:17:06.442
you feel like
giving up on life altogether.

185
00:17:06.525 --> 00:17:10.112
I said stop talking!
I won't agree to that!

186
00:17:10.696 --> 00:17:12.781
I won't eat the abalone!

187
00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:18.454
Oh, my little girl.

188
00:17:20.456 --> 00:17:22.166
When will you understand?

189
00:17:33.093 --> 00:17:33.927
Ae-sun,

190
00:17:34.803 --> 00:17:37.598
if you ever feel like giving up on life,

191
00:17:37.681 --> 00:17:40.142
think about my life as a <i>haenyeo.</i>

192
00:17:43.353 --> 00:17:45.272
<i>People who make their living on land</i>

193
00:17:45.355 --> 00:17:48.317
<i>say they want to die so easily</i>
<i>when things get rough.</i>

194
00:17:49.485 --> 00:17:51.361
<i>No matter how upset or agonizing life is,</i>

195
00:17:51.945 --> 00:17:54.573
they can't speak lightly of death
in front of a <i>haenyeo.</i>

196
00:17:55.908 --> 00:17:59.661
<i>I've faced death hundreds of times</i>
<i>in those powerful waters,</i>

197
00:17:59.745 --> 00:18:03.207
<i>and each time, I found</i>
<i>hundreds of reasons to keep living.</i>

198
00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:04.958
So keep on living.

199
00:18:05.584 --> 00:18:06.835
Keep on living.

200
00:18:07.711 --> 00:18:09.713
Why die with so many reasons to live?

201
00:18:12.925 --> 00:18:15.803
When your body's tired
and your heart wants to give up,

202
00:18:16.762 --> 00:18:18.639
there will be days

203
00:18:18.722 --> 00:18:20.599
when you want to give up on life.

204
00:18:21.183 --> 00:18:22.476
Refuse to back down.

205
00:18:23.435 --> 00:18:24.770
Fight to pick yourself back up.

206
00:18:25.354 --> 00:18:27.147
<i>Take out a blanket and stomp on it.</i>

207
00:18:27.231 --> 00:18:28.690
<i>Till your soil.</i>

208
00:18:28.774 --> 00:18:30.192
<i>Go earn your money.</i>

209
00:18:30.776 --> 00:18:34.780
If you tell yourself,
"I won't die. I'm gonna survive,"

210
00:18:34.863 --> 00:18:37.491
<i>and use your arms and legs to push you up,</i>

211
00:18:39.034 --> 00:18:41.370
<i>you'll get past the dark waters</i>

212
00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:44.957
<i>and finally see the sky.</i>

213
00:18:47.835 --> 00:18:49.628
By then, you'll breathe again.

214
00:19:14.862 --> 00:19:17.656
- Do you know how to do it?
- No, I don't.

215
00:19:17.739 --> 00:19:19.074
This will be sweet, right?

216
00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:25.873
Ooh.

217
00:19:26.623 --> 00:19:28.041
Ooh, it looks yummy.

218
00:19:40.637 --> 00:19:42.556
Is that what you wanted to eat?

219
00:19:45.684 --> 00:19:47.769
Is that the food you craved?

220
00:19:52.524 --> 00:19:54.568
Hey, speak to me. What's going on?

221
00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:57.905
Are you mad at Mommy?

222
00:20:43.617 --> 00:20:44.952
Yang Eun-myeong.

223
00:20:45.619 --> 00:20:47.955
I asked you why you won't talk to me, son.

224
00:20:51.667 --> 00:20:53.794
Never gonna talk to me again, is that it?

225
00:21:27.995 --> 00:21:31.790
SCHOOL SUPPORT FEES DUE BY THE 20TH

226
00:21:47.180 --> 00:21:49.433
Why didn't you say
you got a perfect score?

227
00:21:51.435 --> 00:21:53.687
Why'd you keep it a secret from me, honey?

228
00:22:00.110 --> 00:22:01.653
Geum-myeong.

229
00:22:04.698 --> 00:22:05.532
Hey.

230
00:22:06.408 --> 00:22:07.617
Are you mad at Mommy?

231
00:22:08.327 --> 00:22:10.329
So mad you won't say anything?

232
00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:12.873
Is it because…

233
00:22:14.875 --> 00:22:16.043
is it because…

234
00:22:19.755 --> 00:22:21.340
…I didn't save your little brother?

235
00:22:22.883 --> 00:22:25.385
Are you mad at me?
Is that why you're not talking?

236
00:22:27.346 --> 00:22:29.514
It's because <i>you </i>are mad at me, Mom.

237
00:22:32.392 --> 00:22:33.393
What?

238
00:22:34.311 --> 00:22:36.480
I left my brother alone.

239
00:22:37.522 --> 00:22:39.107
That's why he's dead.

240
00:22:48.533 --> 00:22:49.368
It's 'cause…

241
00:22:50.827 --> 00:22:51.995
it's 'cause

242
00:22:53.330 --> 00:22:55.207
I went out there on the bike.

243
00:22:55.957 --> 00:23:00.003
If I never left to ride the bike,
Dong-myeong would still be alive.

244
00:23:00.087 --> 00:23:01.338
It's 'cause

245
00:23:02.547 --> 00:23:05.342
I wouldn't listen when I was told not to

246
00:23:06.510 --> 00:23:08.637
because a typhoon was coming.

247
00:23:09.137 --> 00:23:13.016
Dong-myeong died
because I still went to go riding.

248
00:23:17.729 --> 00:23:18.897
<i>That was when</i>

249
00:23:20.148 --> 00:23:21.358
<i>Mom and Dad</i>

250
00:23:22.359 --> 00:23:24.069
<i>came to their senses.</i>

251
00:23:28.990 --> 00:23:30.033
I'm sorry.

252
00:23:31.618 --> 00:23:32.786
I'm so sorry.

253
00:23:33.995 --> 00:23:34.871
I'm sorry.

254
00:23:36.248 --> 00:23:37.541
It's all my fault.

255
00:23:38.458 --> 00:23:39.918
I'm sorry, Eun-myeong.

256
00:24:10.407 --> 00:24:11.241
I'll do it.

257
00:24:14.828 --> 00:24:18.415
<i>The Steelheart</i>
<i>picked himself up after three days.</i>

258
00:24:18.498 --> 00:24:20.500
<i>He finished his breakfast</i>

259
00:24:21.751 --> 00:24:23.253
<i>and went out to sea.</i>

260
00:24:24.337 --> 00:24:25.338
Hmm.

261
00:24:38.435 --> 00:24:40.937
Geum-myeong, tell your teacher

262
00:24:41.938 --> 00:24:44.566
I'll pay your school fees
in three days, okay?

263
00:24:50.363 --> 00:24:51.198
Hmm?

264
00:24:53.867 --> 00:24:57.037
<i>They had three days</i>
<i>to mourn. That's all.</i>

265
00:24:58.747 --> 00:25:00.332
<i>Only three days.</i>

266
00:25:04.544 --> 00:25:08.048
Dad,
what are you gonna catch today?

267
00:25:08.673 --> 00:25:09.508
Croaker.

268
00:25:10.467 --> 00:25:11.343
Summer croaker.

269
00:25:12.511 --> 00:25:14.262
- Croaker?
- Mm.

270
00:25:15.138 --> 00:25:17.390
I'll bring them home
instead of selling them.

271
00:25:18.183 --> 00:25:19.476
- Bring them back?
- Yeah.

272
00:25:21.102 --> 00:25:21.937
Let's

273
00:25:22.771 --> 00:25:24.022
all eat together tonight.

274
00:25:25.232 --> 00:25:27.150
Let's all eat together as a family.

275
00:26:20.620 --> 00:26:22.330
Wanna come eat with us?

276
00:26:22.414 --> 00:26:24.624
She sold everything.
She's packing up.

277
00:26:25.542 --> 00:26:29.212
Well, she has her back to the sea,
but business is good.

278
00:26:30.630 --> 00:26:34.009
She says that
she doesn't want to even look at the sea.

279
00:26:35.635 --> 00:26:37.596
The skies are so clear today.

280
00:26:38.430 --> 00:26:39.889
Seeing it this clear,

281
00:26:40.557 --> 00:26:44.060
as if nothing ever happened,
makes her want to vomit.

282
00:26:48.440 --> 00:26:52.569
Her mother, her father,
and now the sea takes her son.

283
00:26:52.652 --> 00:26:55.113
Imagine how she feels
earning a living at the sea.

284
00:26:55.196 --> 00:26:56.072
Goddamn.

285
00:26:57.782 --> 00:27:00.660
She has to live
with all of that heartache.

286
00:27:02.912 --> 00:27:05.915
The sea god is a sadistic one.

287
00:27:05.999 --> 00:27:08.251
He stole everything she held dear

288
00:27:08.918 --> 00:27:11.254
but tells her,
"I'll keep you alive, I think."

289
00:27:12.005 --> 00:27:14.341
So he still gives her all kinds of things.

290
00:27:14.841 --> 00:27:16.343
I'm thankful to her.

291
00:27:17.427 --> 00:27:19.596
I'm thankful she's moving on.

292
00:27:20.805 --> 00:27:22.599
Did you sell all the squid?

293
00:27:23.558 --> 00:27:25.602
We managed to catch
a convict grouper today.

294
00:27:26.353 --> 00:27:30.398
If we sell that one,
we can get 1,000 won, easy.

295
00:27:35.070 --> 00:27:37.197
We can even buy Eun-myeong a new backpack.

296
00:27:37.947 --> 00:27:39.783
It's so unfair.

297
00:27:45.205 --> 00:27:46.831
So unfair.

298
00:27:55.423 --> 00:27:57.300
Geum-myeong. Eun-myeong. Let's go.

299
00:28:14.359 --> 00:28:16.027
I don't wanna be

300
00:28:17.612 --> 00:28:19.948
around the sea for any reason at all.

301
00:28:21.866 --> 00:28:24.285
It's so unfair.

302
00:28:27.997 --> 00:28:28.832
Ae-sun,

303
00:28:30.667 --> 00:28:31.835
let's stop crying.

304
00:28:34.462 --> 00:28:36.089
If Mom and Dad keep crying,

305
00:28:37.215 --> 00:28:38.258
it'll affect the kids.

306
00:28:39.175 --> 00:28:40.635
They'll always be anxious.

307
00:28:41.386 --> 00:28:44.431
I want this summer to be over already.

308
00:28:46.057 --> 00:28:48.226
Pretty annoying how erratic it is.

309
00:28:49.686 --> 00:28:51.646
If it's hot, it's way too hot.

310
00:28:52.480 --> 00:28:54.441
When it rains, it pours.

311
00:28:56.151 --> 00:28:59.070
Summer lets nature grow lush,
but the next thing you know,

312
00:28:59.738 --> 00:29:03.283
it brings storms and crushes everything,
and we're helpless.

313
00:29:04.033 --> 00:29:05.702
<i>The two-faced summer</i>

314
00:29:06.286 --> 00:29:08.163
<i>brought my young parents</i>

315
00:29:08.246 --> 00:29:09.831
<i>down to their knees.</i>

316
00:29:10.874 --> 00:29:13.334
Why does it have to be so aggressive?

317
00:29:14.627 --> 00:29:17.005
If it were me, I'd cut me some slack.

318
00:29:17.088 --> 00:29:19.174
Hey, watch out for that hole there.

319
00:29:19.257 --> 00:29:20.425
No problem.

320
00:29:20.508 --> 00:29:22.135
We all give beginners a break.

321
00:29:24.429 --> 00:29:26.055
But it's a first for me too.

322
00:29:28.600 --> 00:29:30.935
Why am I not getting a break
from the sea god?

323
00:29:32.103 --> 00:29:35.190
<i>Like grass</i>
<i>that was pressed down by the typhoon…</i>

324
00:29:35.690 --> 00:29:37.358
How can we move on now?

325
00:29:38.485 --> 00:29:41.404
<i>…she was knocked down,</i>
<i>but she got back up again.</i>

326
00:29:41.488 --> 00:29:42.530
Still,

327
00:29:43.573 --> 00:29:45.825
life goes on despite the summer's whims.

328
00:29:48.453 --> 00:29:51.414
Grass and trees that are knocked down
by the summer typhoon,

329
00:29:52.582 --> 00:29:53.666
they'll get up again.

330
00:29:56.336 --> 00:29:58.880
Rain can fall
and just sweep away everything.

331
00:30:00.965 --> 00:30:03.218
Ah, but once the sun shines again,

332
00:30:04.302 --> 00:30:05.929
everything comes back to life.

333
00:30:06.429 --> 00:30:08.139
All things on land and sea.

334
00:30:12.393 --> 00:30:13.853
What if I can't move on?

335
00:30:16.689 --> 00:30:19.943
I think moving on
could be a thing I can't do.

336
00:30:23.071 --> 00:30:24.656
There are crabs here.

337
00:30:24.739 --> 00:30:25.907
Our kids need to live on.

338
00:30:25.990 --> 00:30:27.367
- Where?
- Here.

339
00:30:27.450 --> 00:30:29.160
You can't catch that one.

340
00:30:35.166 --> 00:30:36.167
Gwan-sik.

341
00:30:43.174 --> 00:30:44.676
I have caused it all.

342
00:30:46.344 --> 00:30:48.137
I was the one who put…

343
00:30:52.141 --> 00:30:53.852
Dong-myeong on the seawall.

344
00:31:03.903 --> 00:31:06.948
On his first birthday,
I carried him on my back or in my arms

345
00:31:07.031 --> 00:31:09.284
so we could all meet you on that seawall.

346
00:31:12.161 --> 00:31:14.706
I lined up the kids and told them,

347
00:31:16.332 --> 00:31:18.835
"If we stand up here, Dad will come soon."

348
00:31:23.214 --> 00:31:25.425
I said no matter how bad the storm is…

349
00:31:27.552 --> 00:31:29.679
you would return to us if we waited there.

350
00:31:39.397 --> 00:31:41.024
I told them that.

351
00:31:45.361 --> 00:31:47.030
Our baby, Dong-myeong…

352
00:31:51.910 --> 00:31:53.244
…died because of me.

353
00:32:00.960 --> 00:32:02.170
It's all my fault.

354
00:32:08.676 --> 00:32:11.554
If you have to assign blame,
then look to the heavens and sea instead.

355
00:32:17.644 --> 00:32:19.187
It's not your fault at all.

356
00:32:19.270 --> 00:32:20.855
Hmm?

357
00:32:22.774 --> 00:32:25.193
Look, nobody in our family
is to blame. No one.

358
00:32:27.195 --> 00:32:30.114
<i>Dad kept telling himself</i>
<i>no one was to blame,</i>

359
00:32:30.198 --> 00:32:33.034
<i>but on the inside, he did resent someone.</i>

360
00:32:34.577 --> 00:32:37.664
<i>Mom said she found out</i>
<i>who it was Dad resented</i>

361
00:32:38.164 --> 00:32:40.041
<i>about 30 years later.</i>

362
00:32:48.299 --> 00:32:49.133
Hey.

363
00:32:49.634 --> 00:32:51.344
ENDOSCOPY CENTER

364
00:32:51.427 --> 00:32:54.389
Do you know what it is your dad uttered?

365
00:32:57.392 --> 00:32:58.977
Um, he muttered nonsense or what?

366
00:32:59.727 --> 00:33:01.521
People do that in endoscopy.

367
00:33:07.151 --> 00:33:10.238
What, did he talk about
another woman?

368
00:33:15.284 --> 00:33:16.327
Barrier.

369
00:33:17.578 --> 00:33:18.871
Huh? Barrier?

370
00:33:19.998 --> 00:33:20.832
<i>Gwan-sik!</i>

371
00:33:21.582 --> 00:33:23.167
Gwan-sik!

372
00:33:23.251 --> 00:33:25.837
<i>He was muttering the words,</i>

373
00:33:27.505 --> 00:33:30.008
<i>"I shouldn't have gone</i>
<i>to build the barrier."</i>

374
00:33:30.967 --> 00:33:32.385
<i>"I shouldn't have gone."</i>

375
00:33:36.097 --> 00:33:39.434
He's very much like steel
in every way.

376
00:33:40.018 --> 00:33:42.353
Once something truly gets into the man,

377
00:33:42.437 --> 00:33:44.439
he just locks it inside.

378
00:33:46.065 --> 00:33:47.650
I don't know how he coped with it.

379
00:33:48.693 --> 00:33:50.486
How did he cope with all that?

380
00:33:54.532 --> 00:33:55.950
Should he have packed it in?

381
00:33:57.076 --> 00:34:01.748
Uh-uh, there were still
two pairs of twinkling eyes watching us.

382
00:34:04.542 --> 00:34:06.627
So we saved both you and Dad?

383
00:34:07.545 --> 00:34:09.005
Absolutely, you did.

384
00:34:10.339 --> 00:34:11.674
You did save us.

385
00:34:17.555 --> 00:34:19.474
<i>If it weren't for you…</i>

386
00:34:20.391 --> 00:34:21.934
<i>If it weren't you…</i>

387
00:34:23.269 --> 00:34:26.647
NAME OF THE DECEASED: YANG DONG-MYEONG

388
00:34:32.445 --> 00:34:36.240
HOUSEHOLDER: YANG GWAN-SIK

389
00:34:37.992 --> 00:34:41.579
RELATIONSHIP TO HOUSEHOLDER: SON

390
00:34:46.459 --> 00:34:49.879
DATE OF BIRTH: SEPTEMBER 6, 1974

391
00:34:54.342 --> 00:34:59.055
3 YEARS OLD

392
00:35:21.828 --> 00:35:25.248
<i>You can't imagine</i>
<i>what it feels like to lose a child.</i>

393
00:35:29.919 --> 00:35:32.588
<i>He couldn't cry openly anywhere.</i>

394
00:35:33.422 --> 00:35:36.092
<i>He was completely broken on the inside.</i>

395
00:35:50.314 --> 00:35:52.692
<i>Dalgona </i>doesn't have much nutrition.

396
00:35:55.820 --> 00:35:57.572
I ate my food. I promise I did.

397
00:35:57.655 --> 00:35:59.949
Jeez, here.

398
00:36:07.707 --> 00:36:11.085
<i>Oh,</i>
<i>I wondered how we could move on.</i>

399
00:36:12.295 --> 00:36:14.755
What in the world did he eat?

400
00:36:18.551 --> 00:36:20.386
Mom, I've been eating every day.

401
00:36:20.469 --> 00:36:22.763
They even bring us meat most of the time.

402
00:36:32.231 --> 00:36:34.150
<i>We were able to move on</i>

403
00:36:34.233 --> 00:36:38.029
<i>because there were people</i>
<i>who fed the children for us.</i>

404
00:36:40.531 --> 00:36:42.700
<i>A canola flower never blooms by itself.</i>

405
00:36:42.783 --> 00:36:45.203
<i>You always see a field of canola flowers.</i>

406
00:36:45.703 --> 00:36:47.163
<i>Had I been on my own,</i>

407
00:36:47.246 --> 00:36:49.415
<i>I would've been broken</i>
<i>a hundred times over.</i>

408
00:36:54.629 --> 00:36:57.340
<i>You know,</i>
<i>as the saying goes,</i>

409
00:36:58.216 --> 00:37:01.636
<i>it takes a village</i>
<i>to keep one person alive.</i>

410
00:37:15.107 --> 00:37:18.694
They're fine. They'll be fine.
With the stove on, they're okay, I think.

411
00:37:23.324 --> 00:37:24.951
Don't make it too obvious.

412
00:37:25.034 --> 00:37:26.994
They might not like
all that kindness and help.

413
00:37:27.078 --> 00:37:28.871
Should we not give them those?

414
00:37:28.955 --> 00:37:30.539
They're today's first eggs.

415
00:37:32.500 --> 00:37:34.710
Give them the first eggs,
then they'll give them strength.

416
00:37:35.211 --> 00:37:37.880
Don't keep me
from giving them eggs.

417
00:37:37.964 --> 00:37:40.341
You're the one
who gave away all of our rice.

418
00:37:40.424 --> 00:37:42.969
You gave them all our octopuses. You did!

419
00:37:49.475 --> 00:37:52.770
So I was wondering
if I could get a little…

420
00:37:54.480 --> 00:37:55.731
…rice, you know.

421
00:37:55.815 --> 00:37:57.858
I don't understand.
What are you saying, dear?

422
00:37:57.942 --> 00:38:00.236
What are you complaining about?

423
00:38:00.319 --> 00:38:02.280
There's plenty of folks worse off.

424
00:38:10.496 --> 00:38:11.622
But is it you?

425
00:38:12.999 --> 00:38:14.041
The rice jar?

426
00:38:15.334 --> 00:38:18.671
Well, I have no idea what you mean,
crybaby woman.

427
00:38:21.632 --> 00:38:25.177
Why are you saying
you don't have any idea? I know you do.

428
00:38:25.261 --> 00:38:29.765
'Cause, for some reason,
that empty jar is never completely empty.

429
00:38:37.857 --> 00:38:40.651
<i>I saw that the rice jar</i>
<i>was empty before I slept.</i>

430
00:38:40.735 --> 00:38:42.403
<i>I know what I saw.</i>

431
00:38:56.083 --> 00:38:59.128
<i>Every morning,</i>
<i>there's a little more, then a little more.</i>

432
00:38:59.211 --> 00:39:00.046
Hmm?

433
00:39:00.921 --> 00:39:04.050
<i>I thought maybe I didn't see very well</i>
<i>because it was night,</i>

434
00:39:04.133 --> 00:39:06.469
<i>but it went beyond a day or two.</i>

435
00:39:06.552 --> 00:39:09.055
<i>There's just enough for a family of three.</i>

436
00:39:09.555 --> 00:39:11.349
<i>It's just so strange.</i>

437
00:39:12.058 --> 00:39:14.560
<i>Just enough to keep us guessing.</i>

438
00:39:14.643 --> 00:39:16.187
<i>It's the exact amount we need.</i>

439
00:39:19.648 --> 00:39:20.941
Oh, why do I bother?

440
00:39:21.567 --> 00:39:22.902
Why do I bother?

441
00:39:27.198 --> 00:39:29.492
It's not some magical jar,

442
00:39:29.575 --> 00:39:30.576
and I'm not a dummy.

443
00:39:30.659 --> 00:39:32.578
She got a migraine figuring it out.

444
00:39:32.661 --> 00:39:35.873
If she just gave it to you,
you wouldn't take it, Ae-sun.

445
00:39:35.956 --> 00:39:40.211
So then she really tried to give it
without you knowing about it.

446
00:39:40.294 --> 00:39:42.338
Um, but… Well, if it gave her a migraine--

447
00:39:42.421 --> 00:39:45.800
Who would want to watch
a pregnant woman go hungry?

448
00:39:49.720 --> 00:39:51.347
Go steam the octopuses.

449
00:39:51.430 --> 00:39:53.099
Somebody gave them to me.

450
00:39:54.266 --> 00:39:57.311
You absolutely don't have to do this
for my mom's ancestral rites.

451
00:39:57.395 --> 00:40:01.107
If you don't add octopus to her table,
your mom will come beat you down.

452
00:40:02.400 --> 00:40:05.152
No <i>haenyeo </i>goes diving by herself.

453
00:40:05.778 --> 00:40:07.071
When you're about to

454
00:40:07.571 --> 00:40:10.116
lose your breath in the deep, dark waters,

455
00:40:10.199 --> 00:40:13.661
well, you have got to be
very near other divers.

456
00:40:13.744 --> 00:40:16.205
Otherwise, you won't be able
to breathe again.

457
00:40:17.081 --> 00:40:19.125
No one's an island.
Let's go together.

458
00:40:19.208 --> 00:40:20.918
If you go with others,

459
00:40:21.001 --> 00:40:23.587
a hundred miles
will feel like ten miles, my dear.

460
00:40:23.671 --> 00:40:29.760
GO TOGETHER, WITH OTHERS.
IF YOU DO, 100 MILES WILL FEEL LIKE TEN.

461
00:40:35.433 --> 00:40:37.810
Gyeong-ja, that is Ae-sun's.

462
00:40:39.687 --> 00:40:41.564
Ae-sun is having the baby soon.

463
00:40:41.647 --> 00:40:43.190
I'm gonna give it to her.

464
00:40:43.274 --> 00:40:45.526
I wanted to touch it a bit
because it has been a while,

465
00:40:45.609 --> 00:40:48.237
so I just wanted
to feel it a little. There.

466
00:40:48.320 --> 00:40:50.698
Right? They're pretty.

467
00:40:52.116 --> 00:40:54.785
- Oh, she is something, isn't she?
- Hey, did you rinse this?

468
00:40:54.869 --> 00:40:56.036
It's so cold.

469
00:40:58.664 --> 00:41:01.792
Can you write
"For Moral Support"?

470
00:41:02.877 --> 00:41:05.754
If you write that for me,
she'll definitely get it.

471
00:41:12.803 --> 00:41:16.765
"For Moral Support," okay?
Hmm? Mm-hmm.

472
00:41:21.187 --> 00:41:22.438
Works for you?

473
00:41:22.521 --> 00:41:25.941
DO HUI-JEONG SCHOLARSHIP
10,000 WON

474
00:41:28.444 --> 00:41:29.737
Is it wrong?

475
00:41:29.820 --> 00:41:32.907
Three months of rent
to go to the baby's family, right?

476
00:41:43.125 --> 00:41:44.502
Can you read, lady?

477
00:41:49.715 --> 00:41:51.342
One, two, three, four.

478
00:41:51.425 --> 00:41:53.135
One, ten, hundred, thousand.

479
00:41:55.387 --> 00:41:56.764
Fine, yes.

480
00:41:56.847 --> 00:41:57.723
Makes sense.

481
00:42:05.022 --> 00:42:05.856
If only

482
00:42:07.066 --> 00:42:08.984
I'd never hidden in that small closet.

483
00:42:09.068 --> 00:42:09.902
Ah shit.

484
00:42:09.985 --> 00:42:12.029
Why did you pay their rent, huh?

485
00:42:12.947 --> 00:42:16.867
It's my destiny to live with
overly giving boss ladies, I guess.

486
00:42:18.202 --> 00:42:20.079
Should you be saying that? Huh?

487
00:42:20.162 --> 00:42:21.163
Sure, why not?

488
00:42:21.247 --> 00:42:23.791
I deserve to be slapped
for what I've done back then,

489
00:42:24.291 --> 00:42:26.168
but you're not guilty of anything.

490
00:42:26.252 --> 00:42:27.753
Since when is love a sin?

491
00:42:28.837 --> 00:42:31.131
Just cut the nonsense

492
00:42:31.215 --> 00:42:34.093
and straighten your priorities out,
all right?

493
00:42:34.176 --> 00:42:36.387
There's nothing complicated about karma.

494
00:42:36.470 --> 00:42:38.013
Animals bring up animals.

495
00:42:38.097 --> 00:42:39.932
Nobles breed nobles, huh?

496
00:42:40.015 --> 00:42:43.769
Kids inherit
their parents' imperfections exactly.

497
00:42:43.852 --> 00:42:46.188
Min-ok, stop.

498
00:42:46.772 --> 00:42:48.232
She must've really hated me.

499
00:42:49.191 --> 00:42:52.319
Her adolescence was ruined
once I joined the family.

500
00:42:52.403 --> 00:42:55.823
It's pretty sneaky of me to think
I can make it up to her with 10,000 won.

501
00:42:55.906 --> 00:42:58.909
- I gave her a whole cabbage field, okay?
- Oh, that rock field, right?

502
00:42:58.993 --> 00:42:59.952
That field of dog shit?

503
00:43:00.035 --> 00:43:03.038
It was Ae-sun's small hands
that plowed that field.

504
00:43:03.122 --> 00:43:04.248
And on top of that,

505
00:43:04.331 --> 00:43:07.293
that field's original owner
was her mother, Byeong-cheol.

506
00:43:08.294 --> 00:43:09.211
Min-ok.

507
00:43:09.295 --> 00:43:11.547
Talk the shit you want,
but keep your conscience straight.

508
00:43:11.630 --> 00:43:13.090
Yapping doesn't justify a thing.

509
00:43:13.173 --> 00:43:15.968
Min-ok, I told you to quit it.
I'm getting angry.

510
00:43:17.052 --> 00:43:18.804
Now that I've raised our kids,

511
00:43:18.887 --> 00:43:20.764
you should've paid for all of

512
00:43:21.265 --> 00:43:23.892
Ae-sun's college tuition
because she truly deserved it.

513
00:43:23.976 --> 00:43:26.395
Ooh! Come on, yeah, college!

514
00:43:26.478 --> 00:43:27.730
Go! Go! Go!

515
00:43:28.314 --> 00:43:29.898
She can go now if she wants.

516
00:43:29.982 --> 00:43:32.192
I'll pay for her,
even if I have to take out a loan!

517
00:43:32.276 --> 00:43:35.321
Why would she go to college now?
How? By what means?

518
00:43:35.404 --> 00:43:38.699
Hey, if she gets in,
I'll pay her tuition. Tell her!

519
00:43:39.658 --> 00:43:41.827
Don't say anything if she doesn't get in.

520
00:43:41.910 --> 00:43:45.205
She doesn't need college to be a captain,
a deputy chief, or anything like that.

521
00:43:46.540 --> 00:43:49.209
If she goes to Seoul,
she'll only be cut down to size.

522
00:43:49.752 --> 00:43:52.421
The best she'll get
is a doctorate.

523
00:43:52.504 --> 00:43:54.173
She'll just drain the family's wallet.

524
00:43:54.256 --> 00:43:57.801
All we'll do is hang banners around town
to show off which college accepted her.

525
00:43:57.885 --> 00:43:59.678
I never saw the big deal anyway.

526
00:44:02.306 --> 00:44:04.099
Hi, Geum-myeong.

527
00:44:07.603 --> 00:44:09.229
Oh, oh, it's her.

528
00:44:13.317 --> 00:44:15.235
Did you make it?

529
00:44:15.861 --> 00:44:16.987
Did you not?

530
00:44:17.738 --> 00:44:19.448
Oh, Mom.

531
00:44:19.531 --> 00:44:21.784
If I didn't get in, who would?

532
00:44:23.369 --> 00:44:24.828
Look, look, look!

533
00:44:24.912 --> 00:44:27.247
"Yang Geum-myeong." It's written here.

534
00:44:28.957 --> 00:44:30.417
Oh my God. Wow.

535
00:44:32.753 --> 00:44:35.130
Hey! Sell the boat! Sell it!

536
00:44:37.800 --> 00:44:40.302
You did it. You did it for real, honey.

537
00:44:42.971 --> 00:44:46.767
I… don't know
if it's okay for me to say this.

538
00:44:46.850 --> 00:44:48.143
I never

539
00:44:49.478 --> 00:44:52.523
thought that I would say this ever again.

540
00:44:53.315 --> 00:44:55.192
- I…
- You're glad?

541
00:44:58.112 --> 00:44:58.946
Yes.

542
00:45:00.030 --> 00:45:01.573
I'm feeling so happy.

543
00:45:04.284 --> 00:45:05.786
So glad.

544
00:45:08.706 --> 00:45:09.915
CERTIFICATE OF ADMISSION

545
00:45:09.998 --> 00:45:13.502
Okay, one, two, three.

546
00:45:14.461 --> 00:45:15.295
Ah!

547
00:45:18.006 --> 00:45:19.174
BOARDING HOUSE AVAILABLE

548
00:45:19.258 --> 00:45:20.384
AFFORDABLE ROOM FOR RENT

549
00:45:20.467 --> 00:45:21.802
RENT NEAR SNU
AFFORDABLE ROOM

550
00:45:24.763 --> 00:45:26.807
Geum-myeong! Geum-myeong!

551
00:45:38.610 --> 00:45:40.487
Your daughter's name is Geum-myeong?

552
00:45:40.571 --> 00:45:42.823
We have one in our family.

553
00:45:44.867 --> 00:45:46.618
Your son's name is Geum-myeong?

554
00:45:46.702 --> 00:45:47.911
Oh, no.

555
00:45:47.995 --> 00:45:48.954
It's me.

556
00:45:49.997 --> 00:45:51.039
I am Geum-myeong.

557
00:45:52.040 --> 00:45:53.417
I'm Park Geum-myeong.

558
00:45:53.500 --> 00:45:55.502
Oh!

559
00:45:58.046 --> 00:46:00.340
Wow, what an interesting coincidence.

560
00:46:00.424 --> 00:46:01.925
YALASHANG FILM CLUB

561
00:46:02.009 --> 00:46:03.218
Should we get some noodles?

562
00:46:03.302 --> 00:46:06.889
So what's your major, huh? What is it?

563
00:46:06.972 --> 00:46:08.474
Oh, um, law.

564
00:46:08.557 --> 00:46:11.769
Let's go have noodles. Hurry up.
Let's take the picture and just go.

565
00:46:11.852 --> 00:46:13.479
Here. I can take it for you.

566
00:46:13.562 --> 00:46:16.064
- If you all want to stand there.
- Ooh, that's nice of you.

567
00:46:16.774 --> 00:46:18.901
Okay, you take ours, and I'll take yours.

568
00:46:18.984 --> 00:46:20.903
Whose picture? Why are you taking theirs?

569
00:46:20.986 --> 00:46:23.071
Let's take it. Come on.

570
00:46:24.406 --> 00:46:26.658
Thank you.

571
00:46:28.118 --> 00:46:28.952
Mm.

572
00:46:29.036 --> 00:46:29.870
Here we go.

573
00:46:30.370 --> 00:46:31.663
One, two, three.

574
00:46:33.791 --> 00:46:35.584
Okay, I'll take one more.

575
00:46:39.171 --> 00:46:40.172
Smile.

576
00:46:42.007 --> 00:46:44.051
One, two, three!

577
00:46:45.260 --> 00:46:46.970
I said I didn't like him.

578
00:46:47.930 --> 00:46:50.140
I told you
I didn't like that guy at all, didn't I?

579
00:46:50.808 --> 00:46:51.850
Why not?

580
00:46:59.733 --> 00:47:01.485
Those weren't intended to be solo shots.

581
00:47:02.069 --> 00:47:05.280
Park Geum-myeong's son
was hitting on Geum-myeong.

582
00:47:05.364 --> 00:47:06.323
Hitting on her!

583
00:47:06.949 --> 00:47:08.325
Okay, I'll take one more.

584
00:47:10.661 --> 00:47:11.703
Okay, smile.

585
00:47:13.622 --> 00:47:16.375
One, two, three.

586
00:47:16.458 --> 00:47:18.335
Oh, so you feel annoyed now?

587
00:47:18.418 --> 00:47:20.087
Hey, let's call Geum-myeong.

588
00:47:20.170 --> 00:47:22.840
Why? You believe they ran off to Busan?

589
00:47:23.423 --> 00:47:24.883
Why would they go to Busan?

590
00:47:24.967 --> 00:47:26.051
Jeez.

591
00:47:26.134 --> 00:47:29.972
You pulled someone else's daughter there,
and you won't let your daughter go?

592
00:47:30.055 --> 00:47:31.598
Oh, I pulled you there?

593
00:47:31.682 --> 00:47:34.142
Jeez, I think you might
have a heart attack

594
00:47:34.226 --> 00:47:36.395
if she ever wanted to get married.

595
00:47:36.478 --> 00:47:38.355
Why would she get married?

596
00:47:46.989 --> 00:47:48.657
I'm telling you ahead of time.

597
00:47:50.534 --> 00:47:51.910
I can't go tomorrow.

598
00:47:54.204 --> 00:47:55.038
Oh.

599
00:47:56.331 --> 00:47:57.165
That's fine.

600
00:47:58.208 --> 00:47:59.626
You have class tomorrow.

601
00:48:01.461 --> 00:48:03.255
No way I can get to Nonsan.

602
00:48:04.131 --> 00:48:05.048
I can't.

603
00:48:07.175 --> 00:48:08.302
Take your mom.

604
00:48:10.804 --> 00:48:11.763
Mm.

605
00:48:12.931 --> 00:48:13.974
It's fine.

606
00:48:15.851 --> 00:48:17.394
Go with Oh Ye-rim.

607
00:48:18.270 --> 00:48:19.479
Why would I go with her?

608
00:48:21.231 --> 00:48:23.817
Anyway, I can't go. You know?

609
00:48:25.319 --> 00:48:26.153
I get it.

610
00:48:27.863 --> 00:48:30.407
- I'm saying I can't go.
- I said I get it.

611
00:48:30.490 --> 00:48:32.200
Damn it, you don't get it.

612
00:48:32.284 --> 00:48:33.702
Well, what do you mean?

613
00:48:34.870 --> 00:48:36.705
What am I saying if I can't go?

614
00:48:39.458 --> 00:48:40.542
Tonight is

615
00:48:41.585 --> 00:48:43.128
our last night together.

616
00:48:44.713 --> 00:48:47.132
Man, it means it's our last night!

617
00:48:48.884 --> 00:48:52.512
<i>Keep her in check.</i>
<i>Your daughter is just like you.</i>

618
00:48:52.596 --> 00:48:54.431
I swear I'm going to, damn it.

619
00:48:54.514 --> 00:48:55.724
What's wrong with you?

620
00:48:56.350 --> 00:48:58.936
<i>A chip off the old block, Oh Ae-sun.</i>

621
00:49:00.437 --> 00:49:03.398
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

622
00:49:07.069 --> 00:49:08.487
Sweetie.

623
00:49:15.744 --> 00:49:17.496
That's nice, isn't it?

624
00:49:18.580 --> 00:49:19.498
Mm.

625
00:49:20.999 --> 00:49:23.752
Is it a lot more expensive
to live on higher floors?

626
00:49:25.796 --> 00:49:27.172
They're full right now, she said.

627
00:49:27.255 --> 00:49:28.590
You believe her?

628
00:49:29.675 --> 00:49:31.551
Well, she's not a sweet talker,

629
00:49:31.635 --> 00:49:32.719
but she's the eldest.

630
00:49:32.803 --> 00:49:35.764
She's always too careful,
even if I tell her not to be.

631
00:49:35.847 --> 00:49:37.015
Jeez.

632
00:49:37.099 --> 00:49:40.102
Why do people in Seoul
have rooms in basements, you think?

633
00:49:40.602 --> 00:49:45.232
Hmm. My heart would break
if my baby was forced to live there.

634
00:49:49.736 --> 00:49:50.862
Will we be able

635
00:49:51.446 --> 00:49:53.031
to sell the cabbage field?

636
00:49:54.533 --> 00:49:56.159
Just leave the field.

637
00:49:57.035 --> 00:49:58.704
But you believe it'll sell?

638
00:49:58.787 --> 00:50:00.247
And stop selling things.

639
00:50:01.665 --> 00:50:03.583
Why? You wanna keep it?

640
00:50:04.334 --> 00:50:06.586
If we sell it all,
you'll have nothing left.

641
00:50:07.087 --> 00:50:10.382
Jeez, your wife over your daughter, huh?

642
00:50:13.635 --> 00:50:15.429
You know, looking back at it all,

643
00:50:16.263 --> 00:50:17.723
those days were nice.

644
00:50:19.016 --> 00:50:20.851
That was the best summer we had.

645
00:50:22.352 --> 00:50:24.646
Everything was so new back then.

646
00:50:25.480 --> 00:50:28.108
Even though it all felt
awkward and difficult,

647
00:50:28.191 --> 00:50:30.235
it was all new and exciting.

648
00:50:31.236 --> 00:50:33.238
I loved everything, you know.

649
00:50:42.914 --> 00:50:44.124
First love,

650
00:50:45.417 --> 00:50:46.626
our honeymoon…

651
00:50:48.628 --> 00:50:50.297
our first house,

652
00:50:50.380 --> 00:50:51.590
first boat,

653
00:50:52.382 --> 00:50:53.216
first full net.

654
00:50:54.301 --> 00:50:56.011
First child.

655
00:50:56.762 --> 00:50:58.513
Having our first child.

656
00:50:59.848 --> 00:51:01.224
Words escape me.

657
00:51:04.853 --> 00:51:06.897
Still leave the cabbage field, Ae-sun.

658
00:51:18.450 --> 00:51:20.452
<i>Just leave the cabbage field.</i>

659
00:51:21.369 --> 00:51:25.082
<i>That field is your reward</i>
<i>for surviving that summer.</i>

660
00:51:28.293 --> 00:51:30.712
<i>I wondered how we could move forward.</i>

661
00:51:32.255 --> 00:51:34.382
<i>But life really just went on.</i>

662
00:51:34.466 --> 00:51:36.718
Hey, Mom, look at this!

663
00:51:36.802 --> 00:51:39.221
<i>Life went on and on.</i>

664
00:51:39.888 --> 00:51:42.808
LIFE GOES ON AND ON

665
00:54:33.228 --> 00:54:37.857
"IN THE HOPE THAT OUR ECHOES
WILL FLOW AND FLOW UNTIL THEY REACH YOU."

